# conversation.xlsx is app content (per-Category "friendly message" copy
# read by app/dash_apps/pages/setup_wizard.py's load_conversation_data),
# not generated/exported data — it must ship with the repo or the Setup
# Wizard silently renders with no guidance banners at all.
!conversation.xlsx
*.json
generate_button_manifest.py
run.log
run_button_audit.py
targeted_audit.py

# LibreOffice/OpenOffice lock files (e.g. ".~lock.SomeFile.xlsx#") — local,
# machine-specific (embeds the OS username and a file:// path), and gets
# created transiently just by having a spreadsheet open. One was
# accidentally committed; never track these.
.~lock.*#
retest_click_failed.py

# Aiven PostgreSQL TLS material + the provisioning script that drops the certs
# on disk. These were committed despite the "secrets are local-only" rule —
# nothing in .gitignore covered *.pem/*.crt/*.key, so a fresh clone handed
# everyone the CA cert and, worse, service.key (the server's own PRIVATE key,
# which is what Postgres uses to authenticate the app to Aiven). Removed from
# the index; the files themselves stay on disk so aiven_db_setup.sh and the
# local psycopg2 ssl connection keep working. Provision fresh material with
# setup_aiven_db.sh on each machine instead of sharing it.
*.pem
*.crt
*.cert
*.key
setup_aiven_db.sh